 "seat": "implementation",
 "instruction": "The file tools in `sanctuary/tools/builtin.py` (`read_file`, `write_file`, `list_directory`) accept any path with no confinement, so a tool argument could read the entity's secrets or overwrite its source. Add a fail-closed sandbox.\n\n- New field `ToolConfig.filesystem_roots: tuple[str, ...] = ()`. The tools read the active config from the module-level `builtin._config` (tests set `builtin._config.filesystem_roots` directly).\n- Resolve every path the three tools touch first (following symlinks and `..`). It must land inside one of the roots; otherwise the tool returns a failed `ToolResult` saying the path is outside the allowed roots. So `../` traversal, an absolute path outside the roots, and a symlink inside a root that points outside it are all denied.\n- With no roots configured, every call fails, with an error saying filesystem access is not configured. A denied write must not create anything.\n- Inside a root, the tools behave exactly as before (including their \"not found\" errors).\n- Add `RunnerConfig.filesystem_roots: tuple[str, ...] = ()` in `sanctuary/api/runner.py`, and pass it into the `ToolConfig` when the runner builds its tool registry with `create_default_registry`.",
